et="gram:siehe"><abbr>s.</abbr></ref></hi> <ref type="entry" target="entry:foreg-ie-ldan">foregieldan</ref>] <hi rend="bold">II</hi>) <hi rend="italic">deutlich <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:mitAccusativ"><abbr>m ac</abbr></ref></hi> [<hi rend="italic">im selben Satze <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:mit"><abbr>mit</abbr></ref> <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Dativ"><abbr>dt</abbr></ref>; <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:siehe"><abbr>s.</abbr></ref> 9 <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:ZeileVorher"><abbr>Z. vorher</abbr></ref></hi>]: fet ~ fét <hi rend="italic">zum <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:Ersatz"><abbr>Ersatz</abbr></ref> <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:fur"><abbr>für</abbr></ref> Füsse</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:El">El</ref> 19; for <ref type="lawCode" target="law:G">G</ref> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:H">H</ref> <hi rend="bold">III</hi>) <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:mitDativ"><abbr>m dt</abbr></ref>, <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:accusativus"><abbr>ac</abbr></ref>? <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:hinter"><abbr>hinter</abbr></ref> <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:regiertem"><abbr>regiertem</abbr></ref> pron</hi> <hi rend="bold">1</hi>) <hi rend="italic">wegen:</hi> þe [bad] ~ genumen sy <hi rend="italic">um wessen Schuld</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Duns">Duns</ref> 3; (<hi rend="italic">Klagen</hi>), þe gebyrige ornest ~ to beonne <hi rend="italic">um deren willen</hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:WiLad">Wl lad</ref> 1 <hi rend="bold">2</hi>) <hi rend="italic">angesichts, vor:</hi> Drihten, þe (<hi rend="italic">in dessen Namen</hi>) þes haligdom is ~ halig <ref type="lawCode" target="law:Swer">Swer</ref> 2; <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:missverstanden"><abbr>missverst.</abbr></ref></hi> <ref type="lawCode" target="law:B">B</ref>; <hi rend="italic">dies lag vor <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:fur"><abbr>für</abbr></ref></hi> pro quo <ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEm">III Em</ref> 1. [<hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:vergleiche"><abbr>Vgl</abbr></ref>. Urk. um</hi> 1060: <hi rend="italic">‘Heilige,</hi> þe seo stow is fore <pb n="75"/>gehalgod’; <ref type="bibl" target="bib:CitThorpeDipl"><hi rend="italic">Thorpe</hi> Dipl. Sax. 391</ref> = <ref type="bibl" target="bib:CitKembleCD"><hi rend="italic">Kemble</hi> Cod. dipl. 1343</ref>]. — <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:ersetztDurch"><abbr>Ersetzt durch</abbr></ref></hi> for <hi rend="italic"><ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:sieheDort"><abbr>s. d.</abbr></ref> und 23, <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:beziehungsweise"><abbr>bezw.</abbr></ref> 13 <ref type="abbreviation" target="gram:ZeileVorher"><abbr>Z. vorher</abbr></ref></hi></dictScrap>
